^SERIES = GSE175332
!Series_title = In Vivo CRISPR Screens Identify E3 Ligase Cop1 as a Modulator of Macrophage Infiltration and Cancer Immunotherapy Target
!Series_geo_accession = GSE175332
!Series_status = Public on May 23 2021
!Series_submission_date = May 22 2021
!Series_last_update_date = May 25 2021
!Series_summary = Cop1 regulates stability of transcription factors. We found that Cop1 can regulate the proteasomal degradation of Cebpd. We generated 4T1 breast cancer cells with CRISPR/Cas9 mediated Cop1 (gene symbol RFWD2) knockout. We used Cebpd antibody to pulldown the DNA fragments binding with Cebpd and did ChIP-seq.
!Series_overall_design = Examination of Cebpd ChIP-seq under two condtions in 4T1 breast cancer cells: Rosa26 and Cop1 knockout. Additionally, we used two different gRNAs to knockout Cop1. Two replicaters per condition.
!Series_type = Genome binding/occupancy profiling by high throughput sequencing
